~ carmillajournalmain1
May 1st, 1878
Earlier in the day when Margaret left the room, I took a peek at her journal that she left open on thy bed. I know I must stray away from peeking into other’s personal belongings, but I could not help myself! I took notice of how she signs her name as M instead of Margaret or even Peggy. Her journal is so put together, I am envious. Whilst I did not read much, I was able to recall her writing about how mundane life is, and how Margaret yearns for something more. I can fulfill her desires! Might I —----------- soon?
-Carmilla~  
=> END

~ carmillajournal2
November 5th, 1878
My parents took me out to go feed, and when I arrived back at the manor I caught Ma—---- being quite suspicious. Ever since Dad opened the Library permanently, —--- and I have been able to read our parents old books. ——was digging behind a certain bookshelf near a closet, and it appears I startled her when I approached. Is there something she is hiding from me? Certainly not! She tells me everything! 
-Carmilla~
=> END

~ carmillajournal3
February 13th, 1879
I am not sure how much longer I can hold in my thirst for___.. Her scent wafts past me too often.. It lingers on my body for longer than I would like to admit.. I know I hath recently turned 14, and I hath yet to find a mate. What if —---- is the one? I hath not had any urges for anyone else but her…
-C.G
=> END

~ carmillajournal4
April 27th, 1879
I, Carmilla Gar——, hath suppressed my urges for my lover ——. I hath taken it upon myself to keep our friendship the way it is at the moment. I shall not ruin our precious bond, no matter what. Her love is pure and kind, warm-hearted and free. Mine love is not so soft.
-C.G.
=> END

